# Case-compat fixtures record byte-exact sha256 digests for their own files
# (e.g. scan/scan_manifest.json hashes scan/metrics.json). A checkout that
# rewrites line endings would turn the recorded "verified" into a false
# "tampered", so these files must be stored and checked out byte-for-byte.
moodify-core-package/tests/fixtures/case_compat/** -text

# The legacy WSE golden case is provenance evidence: its scan manifests record
# byte-exact sha256 digests of the files below as the producing machine wrote
# them (CRLF included). Stored LF-normalized they can never verify off-Windows
# — a normalizing checkout turns recorded evidence into a false tamper report
# (caught by Linux CI 2026-10-09). Keep these bytes exactly as recorded.
examples/golden_case/**/metrics.json -text
examples/golden_case/**/timeline_metrics.jsonl -text
